      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "JIMMY JAMES MAGUIRE NZ (10) was a beaten favourite in a higher-graded race here last time but still performed well, coming from this row to miss by a neck. Had won two in a row at this venue prior. With even luck he'll be tough to hold out. MIKI MOO (8) looks close to a win after placing in her last two outings at Menangle. Another that may be relying on some luck from the second line but this race suits. KAIRAKI DELIGHT NZ (7) hasn't missed the top-four this time in and has the hoof on the till after back-to-back seconds, one of them here when he missed narrowly. Draws for a trail and goes well at this distance. BEV THE GOAT NZ (9) disappointed last time but won prior to add to a good record here so may be worth another chance.",
